    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by stolen base upside against exploitable rotations. Our standout play is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who benefits from a high-leverage leadoff spot against Feltner (xERA 4.69). With a massive +17% boost from the SP skill profile and an elite +14% platoon edge, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our primary engine for SB production. He is closely followed by **Christian Yelich** (74.67), whose matchup against Cecconi also exploits a favorable RHP platoon and slow delivery mechanics, making the top of our order a constant threat to manufacture runs. Meanwhile, **Kyle Schwarber** (69.09) and **Carson Benge** (67.04) offer significant stability; **Kyle Schwarber** continues to thrive on high xwOBA metrics, while **Carson Benge** provides the best combination of park factor and SP matchup leverage, cementing his role as a high-floor producer despite his youth.\n\nOn the bench, **Caleb Durbin** (44.94) remains the most difficult exclusion. While he holds a respectable projection, the high xERA of opposing starter Cease (3.07) significantly neutered his SP Skill adjustment, forcing him below our internal threshold in favor of the higher-ceiling profiles of **Casey Schmitt** (56.89) and **Josh Smith** (53.53). We remain cautious regarding **Yordan Alvarez** (60.65); despite his elite status, his L/L matchup against Valdez results in a -9% platoon penalty, requiring careful monitoring should the game script turn sour. We are currently holding **Junior Caminero** in the #3 spot pending official confirmation; if his lineup position fluctuates, we may need to adjust our sequencing, but his current score suggests he remains a lock unless the weather or late-scratches intervene. While **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** remain on the bench as reserves, their sub-40 efficiency ratings confirm that we have prioritized high-probability starters across the board to navigate today's specific pitching landscape.",
